  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 344 AM MDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nIn the long term the upper level low that was \nresponsible for our rainy weekend and start to the week starts to \npush in the Great lakes region by Tuesday. Tuesday looks rather dry \nas we enter a more zonal westerly flow aloft. This dry westerly flow \nis expected to last until Thursday as agreed upon by the Global \nmodels. However, they are still continuing to trend with another low \npressure system moving into the Pacific Northwest to give us another \npossible Friday and last through the weekend. The models haven't come \nto an agreement on timing and intensity as it tracks through the \nIntermountain West. So while we could still use the moisture for our \nfarms and reservoirs  The details of this system still remain \nundecided.",
